{
  "rules": [
    "Mild positive bias at short horizons (≈D+1 to D+15): model levels tend to run ~0.3–1.2 EUR above realized prices in steady/up markets; apply a small downward level shift early in the path.",
    "Missed late-horizon upside in breakout regimes (≈D+20 to D+30): when spot has recently accelerated upward, the model underestimates the tail (often by ~2–9 EUR by D+28–D+30); add an upward drift/convexity term to the back end when recent 5–10d momentum is strongly positive.",
    "Over-smoothing / lag around turning points: forecasts often keep a gentle mean-reverting/flat profile while realized prices trend more strongly (down mid-horizon in some cases, sharply up late); increase responsiveness to recent trend (higher weight on last 3–7 observations) to reduce lag.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias correction: use a piecewise adjustment—slightly down for D+1..D+15, near-neutral for D+16..D+22, and up for D+23..D+30 conditional on positive momentum/volatility expansion.",
    "Regime trigger heuristic: if last price > 20d MA and the 5d change is positive and large, treat as ‘breakout’ and lift the entire D+20..D+30 segment; otherwise default to the small early-horizon downward bias correction."
  ]
}
